{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"8d2eaea0948c1864f64bce813c9b743ab1839a19ad3cad2ec5dad9e73ce48e5d","digest":{"component_or_area":"audit page renderer","key_entities":["src/rebar/audit/page.py:329","COMPLETION_VERDICT","kind","met","lacking","PASS verdict","criterion"],"problem_keywords":["audit page rendering","completion verdict","criterion kind","lacking flag","operator-attested","non-codebase"],"propositions":["The audit page renders a lacking flag based only on operator-attested criteria but must also accept non-codebase criteria to avoid silently missing un-attested entries after schema changes","The condition at page.py:329 computes lacking as (kind == 'operator-attested' AND not met) and must be widened to include kind == 'non-codebase'","The schema declares kind as an unconstrained string with no enum, and page.py is the sole site in the codebase that validates criterion kind values","Rendering must produce lacking=true for both operator-attested and non-codebase criteria when met=false, and lacking=false for codebase-verifiable criteria regardless of met status"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787342872508610001,"uuid":"7de5c0aa-d84f-4716-bc72-1d1febeb122f"}